## Description

`Round<T>(ReadOnlySpan<T>, int, MidpointRounding, Span<T>)` was missing a `return` after the `digits == 0` early exit, causing the round to execute twice:

```csharp
if (digits == 0)
{
    Round(x, mode, destination);
    // fall-through: entire method continues, rounding again
}
```

Also fixed `break` → `return` in the `AwayFromZero` switch case for consistency with all other cases in the same switch.

